## Model card

- **Name:** GPT-Realtime-2.1
- **Short description:** OpenAI's current flagship Realtime speech-to-speech model — an update to `gpt-realtime-2` (2026-05-07) with better alphanumeric recognition, silence/noise handling and interruption behavior, plus a platform-wide p95 latency cut of at least 25% via improved prompt caching. Distinct from `gpt-realtime-2.1-mini` (the lower-cost distilled sibling) and from the `gpt-live-1` full-duplex Live API line.
- **Provider / access:** OpenAI Realtime API only — `v1/realtime` over WebRTC (browser/mobile), WebSocket (server/telephony via SIP), plus the Playground. Official endpoint table marks Chat Completions, Responses, Live, Batch, Fine-tuning, Transcription and Translation as **not supported**; supported features are `function_calling` and `prompt_caching`.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-07-06 (OpenAI Developer Community announcement "New Realtime models on the API: gpt-realtime-2.1 and gpt-realtime-2.1-mini"; TechTimes 2026-07-07). Knowledge cutoff: Sep 30, 2024 (official model page).
- **IDs:** `gpt-realtime-2.1` (OpenAI). **No OpenCode Zen Free ID** (Zen model list checked 2026-09-29: no `realtime`/`whisper`/`translate` ids) and no OpenRouter listing checked for this report — no free route exists.
- **Context window:** 128,000 tokens, 32,000 max output tokens (official model page `developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-realtime-2.1`).
- **Modalities:** text, audio and image in; text and audio out (official model page). Reasoning yes — configurable effort `minimal / low / medium / high / xhigh`, default `low`, reasoning-token support listed. Tool calls yes (`function_calling`, parallel tool calls with spoken preambles — "reasoning-while-talking"). JSON mode not listed — no verified public confirmation found.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-29):** text in $4.00 / cached $0.40 / out $24.00 per 1M tokens; audio in $32.00 / cached $0.40 / out $64.00 per 1M; image in $5.00 / cached $0.50 per 1M (official announcement table + OpenAI pricing docs). Paid, no free tier; audio pricing is what dominates real session cost (production analyses put the Realtime API near ~$18/hr of voice interaction at scale — TechTimes citing AssemblyAI).
- **Architecture:** proprietary; parameter count, MoE shape and training data not disclosed.

